</section>

<section id="stats">
  <h2>5. Statistical exploration</h2>
  <p>The analysis uses the curve and base point selected in section 3. It computes the public keys <span class="math">Q = kG</span> for <span class="math">k = 1 … K</span>, treats the coordinates as data, and runs the same tests on a Keccak-256 control. When K is larger than the order of G the sequence wraps around, so the counts show how often each point is hit. The default K = 200 is about eleven periods for the order-18 generators of the toy curve.</p>
